# RME post-payment invoice correction — preparation (rule 206)

> **Superseded in part by rule 207 (FEATURE-RME-POSTPAYMENT-INVOICE-CORRECTION-1):**
> post-payment correction is now IMPLEMENTED behind its own default-OFF switch and is
> still NOT ACTIVE. §B, §C and §E below remain in force; rule 207 records what was built.

Labels: **VERIFIED** (read from source or production, this task),
**PROPOSED** (design only, awaiting the owner), **PENDING** (register code still open).
Nothing labelled PROPOSED is policy. Do not implement, enable or report it as active.

Documents: ADR 0012 · `docs/architecture/rme-postpayment-invoice-correction-design.md` ·
`docs/decisions/rme-postpayment-correction-owner-decision-proposals.md` ·
`docs/operations/rme-postpayment-invoice-correction-sop-draft.md` (DRAFT) ·
`docs/sprints/preparation-rme-postpayment-invoice-correction-1.md`.

## A. Status (VERIFIED, 2026-10-25, runtime `20303a5b`)

1. Post-payment correction is **NOT_IMPLEMENTED and NOT_ACTIVE**. Any invoice with a
   payment is refused at submission with `CORRECTION_TYPE_NOT_ENABLED`
   (`prePaymentIneligibility()`); `RmeInvoiceCorrectionType::ENABLED = [PRE_PAYMENT]`.
   The schema already admits `POST_PAYMENT` (CHECK), so enabling it needs no
   correction-table migration — which is exactly why a type flip alone is forbidden.
2. ~~Owner decisions PP-1…PP-10 are **PROPOSED, none approved**.~~ **SUPERSEDED
   2026-10-25 by §F (ratification):** PP-1…PP-10 are `OWNER_POLICY_APPROVED`. D2, D8,
   D9, D12, D13, D14, D15, D17, D23 are answered for post-payment correction only;
   D21c, D21g, D22 stay PENDING; D28 stays the interim Rp0-original guard.
3. Refund, payment reversal, patient credit, Rp0 adjustment, financial settlement
   remain NOT_ACTIVE. The SPN4 pilot (D1c) and identities 29/1 (D1e) are unchanged;
   no reviewer or role gained financial authority.

## B. Foundations a future implementation MUST reuse (VERIFIED)

4. **One correction engine.** Post-payment is a second correction TYPE in
   `RmeInvoiceCorrectionService`, not a parallel service, table or state machine.
5. **Type is derived by the server from the ledger under the invoice lock**
   (`Σ payments > 0` ⇒ `POST_PAYMENT`), never taken from input.
6. **Payment rows are never written by a correction** (rule 189 model guard). A
   correction never creates a payment, refund, reversal or settlement row.
7. **D10 is already type-agnostic** (`RmePaymentService::assertNoActiveCorrection`)
   and **D28 is already type-agnostic** (`zeroOriginalIneligibility`, original from
   v0). Keep both; do not fork them per type.
8. **Lock order:** invoice row `FOR UPDATE` → correction row → (new) obligation row.
   No new lock ahead of the invoice; the visit is not locked by a correction.
9. **The invoice fingerprint already covers payments** (id + amount), status and
   `correction_version`; a payment landing after submission makes the correction
   STALE. Staleness for post-payment must compare the ledger, not "any payment exists".
10. `applyLocked()` asserts `status = UNPAID` and no payment — a post-payment path
    must branch by type, never delete that assertion for pre-payment.
11. Invoice status after a post-payment apply is DERIVED from the ledger with the same
    rule as `RmePaymentService::refreshInvoiceStatus()` (`paid ≥ total ⇒ PAID`, else
    `PARTIAL`) through ONE shared helper.
12. **Overpayment is never a negative receivable and never a negative payment**
    (audit §12). Every receivable consumer clamps or filters (`remainingAmount()`,
    oversight `> 0`, dashboards `max(0, …)`); a new consumer must do the same.
13. **Receipts render from LIVE rows today** (`RmePaymentController::receipt`, PAID
    only). Correcting a PAID invoice would silently change an issued receipt — a
    receipt snapshot (Phase E) is a hard prerequisite of activation (PP-5; D7's
    technical note "no issued receipt is ever invalidated" stops being true).
14. Lab candidates are generated only by the payment path when an invoice becomes
    PAID; D23 refuses correcting an invoice that has candidates (production: #38, #42).

## C. Design — PROPOSED at preparation, **approved policy since 2026-10-25** (§F)

15. Separate default-OFF flag, SPN4 allowlist and identities 29/1 (PP-1); checker 1
    approves = applies atomically, case-specific Owner approval reference (PP-2).
16. A downward correction below the money received records an **overpayment
    obligation atomically** (`OPEN`, server-derived amount `max(0, paid − new total)`),
    never executes a refund; a further correction is refused while an obligation is
    OPEN (PP-3). An upward correction creates an ordinary outstanding balance
    collected at the invoice branch (PP-4, OD-1a).
17. Reporting: cash KPI unchanged; obligations reported separately; attribution to
    the invoice branch (PP-6).

## D. Production evidence recorded, NOT verified (2026-10-25)

18. Read-only measurement found the **first real pre-payment correction**:
    `RMECOR-202610-000001` on invoice #42 (SPN4), Rp6.000.000 → Rp5.000.000, submitted
    by user 29 at 03:20:52 UTC, approved+applied by user 1 at 03:23:22 UTC (v0 + v1
    frozen), then payment #50 Rp5.000.000 → PAID; a lab candidate followed. Also the
    first dispute-reviewer designation (user 11, SPN4, by user 1, 03:21:58 UTC).
19. This rule does **not** state that the case was Owner-approved (the reason text
    carries no recognisable approval reference) and does **not** change Sprint 2's
    status. Only a Sprint 2 closure verification task may evaluate it (design RG-0).

## E. Never

20. Never enable `POST_PAYMENT` by editing `ENABLED`, a config value or an
    environment variable without the recorded owner decisions and the full
    implementation (obligation, receipt snapshot, tests, PG races).
21. Never encode a PP as approved, never invent an Owner approval, signature or
    reference, and never fabricate a case to produce evidence.
22. Never return money outside the system to settle an obligation; never offset an
    obligation against another invoice; never reopen a visit because a total changed.

## F. Ratification (RATIFICATION-RME-POSTPAYMENT-OWNER-DECISIONS-PP1-PP10-1, 2026-10-25)
Evidence: `docs/sprints/ratification-rme-postpayment-owner-decisions-pp1-pp10-1.md`;
register section "Ratification of PP-1 … PP-10".

23. PP-1…PP-10 are `OWNER_POLICY_APPROVED` against their canonical text (owner
    directive in the brief; no signed artefact, none fabricated). Labels stay apart:
    approved ≠ `TECHNICAL_ENFORCEMENT_DEPLOYED`. Post-payment correction remains
    NOT_IMPLEMENTED / NOT_ACTIVE until its feature ships.
24. Each PP names one recommended option and that option is what was approved: PP-3
    is option A (atomic OPEN obligation); option B was offered only "if the Owner wants
    it staged" and was not elected. An implementer never picks an option a decision
    left open — none was.
25. **The case-specific Owner approval reference is MANDATORY for post-payment
    correction** (PP-2, PP-7) and must be enforced in code, not only by procedure —
    Sprint A showed the procedural gate let the first real pre-payment case through
    with no reference at all.
26. D7 extends to issued receipts (PP-5). The receipt snapshot is an ACTIVATION
    prerequisite; a legacy receipt with no snapshot is never presented as an identical
    reprint.
27. Activation is blocked while Sprint 2 is NO_GO (PP-10); flag-OFF implementation is
    allowed. Refund, settlement, reversal and patient credit stay PENDING
    (D4/D5/D6/D18/D25/D26).
28. Sprint A's `HUMAN_SEPARATION=RED_FLAG_UNRESOLVED` concerns accounts 29/1 — the pair
    PP-1 names. It is not a ratification conflict; it is an Owner follow-up that must be
    resolved before any activation relies on the pair.
